\title{aciR: Assimilative Causal Inference for Conditional Gaussian Nonlinear
Systems}
\description{
The aciR package implements assimilative causal inference (ACI) for
conditional Gaussian nonlinear systems (CGNS). A CGNS pairs an observed
signal with an unobserved component whose conditional statistics, given the
observed path, are Gaussian and available in closed form.
}
\details{
The package provides the forward filter (\code{\link[=aci_filter]{aci_filter()}}), the backward
smoother (\code{\link[=aci_smoother]{aci_smoother()}}) and the relative-entropy causal-information
metric (\code{\link[=aci_metric]{aci_metric()}}) that contrasts the smoother posterior against the
filter posterior. These three functions form the numerical core and are
written against a general CGNS components list, so they apply beyond any
single model. The nonlinear dyad model with intermittent extreme events is
supplied as a worked example through \code{\link[=aci_dyad_components]{aci_dyad_components()}} and
\code{\link[=aci_simulate_dyad]{aci_simulate_dyad()}}.

Above the core sits a model layer. \code{\link[=aci_cgns_model]{aci_cgns_model()}} wraps a CGNS in an
\code{aci_model} object, \code{\link[=aci_dyad_model]{aci_dyad_model()}} builds the flagship dyad model,
\code{\link[=aci_simulate]{aci_simulate()}} draws a realisation of a model, and \code{\link[=aci]{aci()}} is the single
entry point that runs the filter, the smoother and the metric together.

The method reimplemented here is due to Andreou, Chen and Bollt (2026).
}
